			"notes": "Mostly tunnels this time.\n\n- Two lines that leave a station side by side now share one double tunnel. Before, each built its own and the frames ended up across the other line's track. Where one of them turns off, there's a junction with the switches and levers in place.\n- A single line turning inside a tunnel gets a real corner instead of bare rock.\n- Short bits of tunnel where a full section doesn't fit, and the corners of double lines, are lined with stone bricks, some cracked and some mossy.\n- Bridges no longer leave a strip of earth hanging over the track where the bank turned out higher than planned.\n- Posts and lamps that lose their ground to a cut come down whole instead of floating, and dirt or rock that a later chunk spills onto a finished line gets cleared. Both turned up while testing with RoadWeaver's roads, and the two mods get along.\n- Admins see a short note when they join if a newer version is out, and a link to the Discord. Both can be switched off in the settings (`updateCheck`, `supportMessage`).\n- The map for new players is off by default now. Turn it on with `starterMap=1`. Servers that already have a config file keep whatever it says.\n- The mod has an icon in Mod Menu and the NeoForge mod list.\n\nThe tunnel changes only show up in land generated after the update.\n\nTake the jar for your loader and Minecraft version:\n\n| Minecraft | Fabric | NeoForge | Paper |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 26.3 | `village-railways-fabric-1.0.1+26.3.jar` | `village-railways-neoforge-1.0.1+26.3.jar` | `village-railways-paper-1.0.1+26.3.jar` |\n| 26.2 | `village-railways-fabric-1.0.1+26.2.jar` | `village-railways-neoforge-1.0.1+26.2.jar` | `village-railways-paper-1.0.1+26.2.jar` |\n| 26.1 | `village-railways-fabric-1.0.1+26.1.jar` | `village-railways-neoforge-1.0.1+26.1.jar` | `village-railways-paper-1.0.1+26.1.jar` |\n| 1.21.11 | `village-railways-fabric-1.0.1+1.21.11.jar` | `village-railways-neoforge-1.0.1+1.21.11.jar` | `village-railways-paper-1.0.1+1.21.11.jar` |\n\nThe Fabric jars need Fabric API. Paper jars go in the `plugins` folder. Players join with a vanilla client and don't need the mod.\n\nQuestions or bugs? Come to [Discord](https://discord.com/invite/X6yxJpk9Fz)."
		},
