			"notes": "The first release. Village Railways links villages with minecart railways built from vanilla blocks while the world generates: stations, open cuts, tunnels, bridges, halts along the way and, if you turn them on, glass tubes under the sea. The [README](https://github.com/valcheffnet/village-railways#readme) has screenshots and all the settings.\n\nTake the jar for your loader and Minecraft version:\n\n| Minecraft | Fabric | NeoForge | Paper |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 26.3 | `village-railways-fabric-1.0.0+26.3.jar` | `village-railways-neoforge-1.0.0+26.3.jar` | `village-railways-paper-1.0.0+26.3.jar` |\n| 26.2 | `village-railways-fabric-1.0.0+26.2.jar` | `village-railways-neoforge-1.0.0+26.2.jar` | `village-railways-paper-1.0.0+26.2.jar` |\n| 26.1 | `village-railways-fabric-1.0.0+26.1.jar` | `village-railways-neoforge-1.0.0+26.1.jar` | `village-railways-paper-1.0.0+26.1.jar` |\n| 1.21.11 | `village-railways-fabric-1.0.0+1.21.11.jar` | `village-railways-neoforge-1.0.0+1.21.11.jar` | `village-railways-paper-1.0.0+1.21.11.jar` |\n\nThe Fabric jars need Fabric API. Paper jars go in the `plugins` folder. Players join with a vanilla client and don't need the mod.\n\nEvery player joining a world for the first time gets one map of the railway network. You can turn that off in the settings.\n\nIn a world you've already played, lines only show up in land you haven't explored yet. If you want them through the old land too, the README explains how; the world gets backed up first.\n\nOn Paper there is no settings screen, so the settings live in `plugins/VillageRailways`, and the player arrow on the big network maps stays at the normal map scale.\n\nQuestions or bugs? Come to [Discord](https://discord.com/invite/X6yxJpk9Fz)."
		}
